    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0463" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg389"/>

                <head>Mr. Pike to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 163.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation.</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">The Hague,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 27, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The horrible news of to-day by telegraph,
                    after two weeks of rejoicing, overwhelms me so completely that I find myself
                    wholly unable to do more than to acknowledge the receipt of your despatches Nos.
                    217 to 224, inclusive.</p>
                <p>With the profoundest emotions of sympathy, and the most agonizing apprehensions
                    for your own condition, I remain, with great respect, your most obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES S. PIKE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
